        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a sonicated methanolic solution (5 mL) of HEP (11.3 μL, 0.1 mmol) and NaOH (4 mg, 0.1 mmol) was added a sonicated solution of L-PGA (16.1 mg, 0.125 mmol) and NaOH (5 mg, 0.125 mmol) in 5 mL MeOH. A 15 mL 1:2 MeOH/MeCN mixture was then added, followed by slow addition, with continuous sonication, of solid Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (12.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) and 3 mL of a methanolic solution of Dy(NO3)3·xH2O (13.6 mg, 0.03 mmol). Slow evaporation without disturbance over ten days afforded blue cube-shaped single crystals of 1L.",
