      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of 1L under 1000 Oe shows χMT = 59.87 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K, decreasing to 24.70 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, consistent with four Dy(III) and eight Cu(II) ions plus depopulation of Stark levels and/or anisotropy. Magnetization at <5 K does not saturate to 7 T; non-superimposable M vs H/T plots indicate anisotropy and/or low-lying excited states. No out-of-phase ac signal at 1000 Hz in zero dc field, so no slow magnetic relaxation (fast quantum tunneling). Solid-state CD of 1L is the enantiomeric reverse of 1D.",
